<title>UK: Societe Generale appoints new London deputy chief.</title>
<headline>Societe Generale appoints new London deputy chief.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Societe Generale said on Wednesday it appointed Christopher Jolly as deputy chief executive of its London branch.</p>
<p>SocGen said Jolly, who previously held the post of executive director, head of corporate banking, would be responsible for corporate banking and financial markets business in London.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
